KONOHAGAKURE — ACADEMY GRADUATION REQUIREMENTS

To graduate the Ninja Academy and be certified as a genin of the Hidden Leaf, a student must satisfy:

1. Written examination — history, chakra theory, tactics, and the shinobi rules.
2. Weapons accuracy — minimum standard in shuriken and kunai throwing.
3. Taijutsu — demonstrated competence in Academy sparring.
4. Ninjutsu — successful performance of the Academy Three, traditionally the Clone Jutsu, before an instructor.

On passing, the graduate receives a Konoha forehead protector and is entered in the registry for genin squad assignment. Exceptional demonstrations of skill may satisfy the ninjutsu requirement by alternative jutsu at instructor discretion (as certified for special cases).

Failure permits re-examination in a later cycle. Graduation certifies readiness for D-rank and supervised C-rank missions.
Issued by the Academy administration.
